{"compatibility":"minor","safety_note_md":"# SafeStan Safety Note

Compatibility: minor.

Protected data: `y_init`, `y`.

Generated files: `model_safe.stan`, `data_safe.json`.

Changes: rewrote the two observed-data likelihoods so each protected top-level data variable appears exactly once on the left-hand side of a built-in sampling statement outside any loop. The column-wise `y_init[k]` and `y[:, k]` lognormal likelihoods were replaced by equivalent vectorized statements using local helper arrays for `log(z_init)`, `log(z)`, and replicated measurement-error scales. The two indexed `theta` prior statements were replaced by one equivalent vectorized prior with deterministic prior-location and prior-scale arrays. No data values were changed or added.
","model_safe_stan":"functions {
  array[] real dz_dt(real t, // time
                     array[] real z,
                     // system state {prey, predator}
                     array[] real theta, // parameters
                     array[] real x_r, // unused data
                     array[] int x_i) {
    real u = z[1];
    real v = z[2];

    real alpha = theta[1];
    real beta = theta[2];
    real gamma = theta[3];
    real delta = theta[4];

    real du_dt = (alpha - beta * v) * u;
    real dv_dt = (-gamma + delta * u) * v;
    return {du_dt, dv_dt};
  }
}
data {
  int<lower=0> N; // number of measurement times
  array[N] real ts; // measurement times > 0
  array[2] real y_init; // initial measured populations
  array[N, 2] real<lower=0> y; // measured populations
}
transformed data {
  array[4] real theta_mu = {1, 0.05, 1, 0.05};
  array[4] real theta_sigma = {0.5, 0.05, 0.5, 0.05};
}
parameters {
  array[4] real<lower=0> theta; // { alpha, beta, gamma, delta }
  array[2] real<lower=0> z_init; // initial population
  array[2] real<lower=0> sigma; // measurement errors
}
transformed parameters {
  array[N, 2] real z = integrate_ode_rk45(dz_dt, z_init, 0, ts, theta,
                                          rep_array(0.0, 0), rep_array(
                                          0, 0), 1e-5, 1e-3, 5e2);
}
model {
  array[2] real log_z_init;
  array[N, 2] real log_z;
  array[N, 2] real sigma_y;

  theta ~ normal(theta_mu, theta_sigma);
  sigma ~ lognormal(-1, 1);
  z_init ~ lognormal(log(10), 1);

  for (k in 1 : 2) {
    log_z_init[k] = log(z_init[k]);
  }
  for (n in 1 : N) {
    for (k in 1 : 2) {
      log_z[n, k] = log(z[n, k]);
      sigma_y[n, k] = sigma[k];
    }
  }

  y_init ~ lognormal(log_z_init, sigma);
  y ~ lognormal(log_z, sigma_y);
}
generated quantities {
  array[2] real y_init_rep;
  array[N, 2] real y_rep;
  for (k in 1 : 2) {
    y_init_rep[k] = lognormal_rng(log(z_init[k]), sigma[k]);
    for (n in 1 : N) {
      y_rep[n, k] = lognormal_rng(log(z[n, k]), sigma[k]);
    }
  }
}
